.TH "tfman" "1" "v3.0.17" ""
.SH "نام (NAME)"
tfman \- Swank manual page browser
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\f[B]tfman\f[R]\ [\f[B]\-h\f[R]]\ [\f[B]\-V\f[R]] [\f[B]\-q\f[R]] files
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
\f[B]tfman\f[R] displays manual pages ala \f[B]man(1)\f[R] using the
Notcurses (\f[B]notcurses(3)\f[R]) terminal UI library.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
\f[B]\-V\f[R]: Print the program name and version, and exit with
success.
.PP
\f[B]\-h\f[R]: Print help information, and exit with success.
.PP
\f[B]\-q\f[R]: Don\[aq]t wait for any input, and don\[aq]t use the
alternate screen.
.PP
files: Files to render.
.PP
If successfully loaded and parsed, the top of the page will be visible.
In the lower right corner is a listing of page sections.
By default, the page browser is in use; press Tab to move between the
page browser and the structure browser.
Press \[aq]s\[aq] to toggle the structure browser\[aq]s visibility.
.PP
\f[B]tfman\f[R] can identify gzipped manual pages, and inflate them on
the fly.
.SH "نکات (NOTES)"
The following keypresses are recognized:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Ctrl\-L\f[R]: Redraw the screen.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]q\f[R]: Quit.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]k\f[R]/\f[B]up\f[R]: Move up by one line.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]b\f[R]/\f[B]pgup\f[R]: Move up by one page.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]h\f[R]/\f[B]left\f[R]: Move up by one section.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]j\f[R]/\f[B]down\f[R]: Move down by one line.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]f\f[R]/\f[B]pgdown\f[R]: Move down by one page.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]l\f[R]/\f[B]right\f[R]: Move down by one section.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]g\f[R]/\f[B]home\f[R]: Go to first line in file.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]s\f[R]: Toggle the structure browser\[aq]s visibility.
.PP
The mouse wheel can also be used to move up and down within the active
browser.
.SH "اشکالات (BUGS)"
\f[B]tfman\f[R] does not currently (and is unlikely to ever) support the
full \f[B]groff\f[R] macro language.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
\f[B]man(1)\f[R], \f[B]notcurses(3)\f[R], \f[B]groff_man(7)\f[R],
\f[B]man\-pages(7)\f[R], \f[B]unicode(7)\f[R]
